// EXPECT: runtime_fail
//OUT: before
//ERR: Error: cannot read file: definitely_missing_file.xyz

// read_file on a missing path is a runtime error — same family as
// division by zero and out-of-bounds indexing. Byte-identical trap on
// both hosts: `Error: cannot read file: <path>` on stdout, exit 1.
// Code that probes for optional files uses file_exists() instead.
print("before");
var s <- read_file("definitely_missing_file.xyz");
print(s);
